Sutrasthana 1
(213)

Among the foods derived from munaka (raisins) and sugarcane products, sugar is included — all these are described as supremely beneficial foods by their natural qualities. Now instruction is given regarding what is extremely harmful: among the husked grains (shuka-dhanya), yavaka (a type of barley preparation) is highly unwholesome; among the legumes (shami-dhanya), black gram (urad) is extremely unwholesome; among unfathomable waters, the river that flows during the rainy season is like collyrium (unfit to drink); among salts, alkali-salt (ushar lavana) is harmful; among vegetables, mustard greens are harmful; among animal meats, cow's meat is the worst among deer-meats; among birds, the black pigeon; among bed-dwelling creatures, the frog; among fish, the chilichima; among ghees, sheep's ghee; among milks, sheep's milk; among solid fats (sthavar sneha), the fat of the kushumbha plant; among the fats of small game animals, the fat of the buffalo; among the fats of fish, the fat of the crocodile; among the fats of aquatic birds, the fat of the crow and the frog; among bulbous roots, the radish; among the fats of grain-eating birds (vishkira), the fat of the sparrow; among the fats of tree-dwelling animals, the fat of the elephant; among fruits, the jackfruit (chhikuch); and among preparations of sugarcane, phanita (a thick molasses) — all of these by their very nature are extremely unwholesome foods. The best varieties among unwholesome food derivatives have been described, as have the wholesome and unwholesome components. Among such food derivatives, medicines of the highest importance — with their classified connections as described in the branches — are now enumerated: among the causes of sustenance, food (anna) is the best; among causes of relief (comfort), water; among fatigue-relievers, wine (sura); among life-promoting substances, milk; among nourishing (brimhana) substances, meat; among appetite-stimulants for food, salt; among heart-pleasing (hridya) substances, sour foods; among strength-promoting substances, the rooster (hen); among aphrodisiacs (vrushya), nakkararet; among pacifiers of kapha-pitta, honey; among pacifiers of vata-pitta, ghee;

Among pacifiers of vata-kapha, oil; among emetics (for kapha), vomiting therapy; among eliminatives for pitta, purgation (virechana); among vata-eliminatives, enema (basti); among agents that promote softness, sudation (fomentation); among agents that promote stability, exercise; among those that damage virility, alkalis; among appetite-restoring substances for disrupted digestion, the tinduka fruit; among those harmful to the throat, raw mango; among those that relieve grief and act as galactagogues, rasa-gathering substances — among these, goat's milk is best; among those that increase kapha and pitta, sheep's milk; among those that produce dreams, buffalo's milk; among those that cause congestion (abhishyanda), foods of slow digestion (mandakadd); among those that are desirable (kushaniya), gavedhuka (a type of wheat grain); among laxatives (virekshana), uha (loosening) food; among diuretics, sugarcane; among those that promote feces, barley (yava); among vata-producers, jamun (Indian blackberry); among producers of kapha-pitta, puri (fried bread); among producers of acid-pitta (amlapitta), horse-gram (kulthi); among producers of kapha-pitta, black gram (urad);

Among adjuvants for emesis, niruha enema, and anuvasana enema, the menafalа fruit is best; among gentle purgatives (sukha-virechana), nisotha; among mild purgatives (mridu virechana), chaturangula; among sharp purgatives (tikshna virechana), the milk of snuhi (euphorbia / thohad); among head-cleansing therapies (shiro-virechana), pratyak-pushpa; among worm-destroyers, vayiwidanga (vidanga); among poison-destroyers, shirisha; among destroyers of itching/skin disease, khadira; among vata-pacifiers, raysana (a rasayana herb); among age-stabilizers (vayasthapaka), amalaka (amla/gooseberry); among wholesome substances, haritaki (chebulic myrobalan); among aphrodisiacs and vata-pacifiers, the root of eranda (castor); among the three — digestive stimulant (dipaniya), digestive (pachaniya), and relief of bloating (anaha-prashaman) — pippalamoola (long pepper root) is best; among agents that relieve rectal pain and swelling (shula and shopha), the root of chitraka (leadwort); among destroyers of hiccup, breathlessness, cough, and flank pain — pushkara-
